Z||000000||Lisa 86 2m4||01-04-2001||11:31 PM||||Hi!<BR>I've been picking up threads here and there about Fiero clubs and a convention? I live in the St. Pete. area, can anyone tell me if there is anything available in this area or how I could find out more? Maybe even Fiero 'specialists' in my area that could be available to bail me out when I insist on trying to fix my car myself.... I would love to have the chance to sit around and discuss all the Fiero possibilities!<BR>Lisa||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cheever2||01-05-2001||12:43 AM||||Sorry took so long to reply, but I was waiting for a Floridian to help you.  Anyway, click this to see an earlier post where I listed the Fiero Club websites.  You may be most interested in the Florida Fiero Council, which is several FL clubs who have associated themselves together under one name... <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/004529.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/004529.html</A> <BR>-<BR>Oh, and welcome to the Forum!<BR><P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I>||||reg||6
Z||000002||RobertVol||01-05-2001||12:54 AM||||Well cheever is right there are a few of us around <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Uh probably the fiero council or even the Central Florida fiero club. <P>Now we have started one here in North FL and would be glad to invite ya to the meetings and trips we are planning in the future. also the one "Convention" that you mentioned  could be the Beloved DAYTONA meeting March 23-25th I believe. I have talked with our club about going together. Check with the clubs closer to you and see if they are doing something similar. The daytona show is one of the BEST. lots of fieros around. <P>Here is a link: <A HREF="http://members.yourlink.net/dragon/daytona2001/" TARGET=_blank>http://members.yourlink.net/dragon/daytona2001/</A> <BR>hope it helps <BR><P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT 56k T TOP  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=819451&a=5959473&p=36934984&Sequence=1"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Lisa 86 2m4||01-05-2001||09:33 AM||||Excellant!! Thanks so much for awesome information! There is a Fiero club that meets just up the road from me in Clearwater! How cool is that!<BR>Thanks again!<BR>Lisa||||reg||1
Z||000004||CozmoPooky||01-05-2001||11:02 AM||||Here is the info on Suncoast Fieros if you don't already have it. Hope to see you there!<P>Meeting held every 2nd Wednesday at 7:00 p.m. <P>Located at Autoway AutoNation Pontiac (formerly Sunset Pontiac) 19320 US Hwy 19N, Clearwater, Florida<P>For more information call:<P>Dave Connelly @ 813-855-4556<BR><P>------------------<BR>CozmoPooky<BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>'87 Duke Coupe<BR>'85 2M6 Targa||||reg||14
